// The detail argument used by 5.2: what it actually takes for a test dataset to deserve
// the word "trustworthy".
//
// Its conclusion is worded *exactly* as the leaf it will replace. That is deliberate and
// it is the one thing the compiler will not check for you. A refinement drops this
// argument into the hole where that leaf was, and its conclusion is the label that
// survives, so if this said something else the argument would quietly start claiming
// something else in that position.

justification trustworthy {

    conclusion claim  is "(R4) The test dataset shall be trustworthy"
    strategy   checks is "The split is disjoint and every label is valid"

    evidence disjoint is "No test row appears in the training split"
    evidence labels   is "Every label is one of the eight Plutchik emotions"

    checks   supports claim
    disjoint supports checks
    labels   supports checks

}
